{"skill":{"slug":"flight-search","displayName":"Flight Search"},"version":{"version":"0.1.7","createdAt":1770362463005,"changelog":"Release 0.1.7","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","size":2173,"sha256":"8ac46d7c366b953b190518ef7adcf3c89c151970a721f5a9f907007e05eb8d12","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","size":1620,"sha256":"69036a304df77868be4cbc3700614f07a5d760bab2899339f7e8037b368e9cc8","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":4361,"sha256":"b875009735aad6c516a982c982966d0da72477a0c04be275e3854c59aa5595ab","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2981,"sha256":"efcb487c7a10f958cc72bc8a46a17d0315e9d6f512ab90f78bac19acb6e2d3af","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"flight_search/__init__.py","size":207,"sha256":"9a86fa6dfdd7d7965efc901c868b36d5a097703b64c5edc7e508bb14aa630c3b","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"flight_search/cli.py","size":8130,"sha256":"0f67b9fdf7de6844a1dbb3e94bbe9a17205b1ebc48e2ca4995a6c66816216cea","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"flight_search/search.py","size":4481,"sha256":"9a99b99e81c1b03d2224b69539bd3bca8df803714073ce4224607063b1567f56","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"install.sh","size":703,"sha256":"3689ff1001837889ad7248a0e24635a59dff4126c53183034944e05d3f93416c","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"pyproject.toml","size":1354,"sha256":"3f506164ff2cc383780a0c2c6b81e8436e2304dcf48af51794944b4753fbeabd","contentType":"application/toml"},{"path":"pytest.ini","size":102,"sha256":"c14b489a30afe60312242394d2e54d37d23e99ccef8d68f203807b76e325c758","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"tests/__init__.py","size":0,"sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"tests/test_cli.py","size":7398,"sha256":"b62c33eb4cc0ee4bb6c79e3bb88d9139cd6f18aae88c3a7a7b05c99efbb64ebe","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"tests/test_search.py","size":7620,"sha256":"2bc7366ae3ce5150ea882d61dabfabe46218eab2778b3bffe5064f27658165d7","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2216,"sha256":"389f4c91bc433ed30d2815f8e1e2b4d8fffc1c4909be73c8cb0cc88d59256f7e","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789036476277,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"fde4fbb3f0ee9f41021a0f50a1f4190c4e917ccc36e2001d95de970e2f3eb6c5","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/fde4fbb3f0ee9f41021a0f50a1f4190c4e917ccc36e2001d95de970e2f3eb6c5","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: flight-search\nVersion: 0.1.7\n\nThe skill is classified as benign. Its primary function is to search Google Flights using the `fast-flights` library, which involves web scraping. The `SKILL.md` provides standard installation instructions for `uv` via `pip`. The `cli.py` file uses `subprocess.run` for a legitimate self-update feature (`--upgrade` flag) that specifically targets the `flight-search` package itself, not arbitrary commands. While `install.sh` and `README.md` contain `curl | bash` instructions for users to install `uv`, these are user-facing instructions and not executed by the OpenClaw agent during skill installation or runtime, as the agent's `SKILL.md` specifies a `pip` installation for `uv`. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, persistence, or prompt injection against the agent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161789014},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":17,"checkedAt":1789036476277},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The flight-search skill mostly does what it says, but its install and update paths can run mutable remote code or upgrade local packages without pinning.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access to Google Flights or the fast-flights library is expected for the stated purpose. The artifacts mention scraping and optional Playwright use in README.md, but SKILL.md does not include a clear privacy notice that itinerary details are sent externally.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"SKILL.md uses package-manager installation, but README.md also documents piping a remote install.sh directly into bash. install.sh itself installs via uv, pipx, or pip, and prints another pipe-to-shell command for installing uv if no package manager is present.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill instructions rely on shell/package-manager execution such as uvx and uv tool install, and README guidance includes an unpinned curl-to-bash installer from a mutable GitHub branch. That is broader authority than needed for a search skill.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"There is no evidence of background services, credential harvesting, or hidden persistence. However, global installation and the explicit --upgrade command can mutate the local Python tool environment and fetch newer unpinned code when invoked.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The core capability is coherent: a CLI wrapper around fast-flights to search Google Flights for routes, dates, fares, airlines, and schedules. The added self-upgrade capability is disclosed but not central to flight search.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review the install path before using this skill. Prefer pinned, standard package-manager installation over the README curl-to-bash command, avoid running --upgrade in managed environments without approval, and assume flight search details such as airports, dates, and passenger counts may be sent to Google or the underlying scraper service.","findings":"[T03] unexpected: Accepted as a real concern for README.md: the documented curl-to-bash installer executes mutable remote content and is not required for flight searching.\n[TM2] unexpected: Accepted in context: piping a downloaded installer to bash is an unsafe installation pattern, although it is documentation rather than automatic runtime behavior.\n[SC2] unexpected: Accepted for the README installer and downgraded for install.sh's uv message because install.sh only prints that third-party command instead of executing it automatically.\n[RA1] unexpected: Partially accepted: --upgrade is disclosed and user-invoked, not hidden self-modification, but it still performs local package mutation outside the core search purpose.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: Accepted: the CLI includes a self-upgrade path that can install newer package code when explicitly requested.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Partially accepted: subprocess package-manager calls are limited to installer detection and explicit upgrade, not ordinary searches, but they broaden the tool's authority.\n[AST4] expected: Downgraded: subprocess calls use argument arrays with shell disabled and no direct shell interpolation; the main concern is environment mutation, not command injection.\n[SQP-2] expected: Partially accepted: sending route/date/passenger details to Google Flights is inherent to the feature, but SKILL.md does not clearly warn about this data flow.\n[RP1] unexpected: Accepted as a supply-chain concern: uvx flight-search and package install examples are unpinned and may run whatever version is current at execution time.\n[LP3] expected: Partially accepted: SKILL.md metadata declares the uvx binary requirement, but it does not narrowly scope shell/package-manager usage beyond that.\n[SC4] expected: Downgraded: pytest is a development dependency and not part of the runtime flight-search path shown in pyproject.toml.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789036476277}}}}}